# Implementation Plan: ResQCore Disaster Response Web Application

Recreate the complete Figma prototype for **ResQCore** (Disaster Response Platform) as a responsive, modern React application using Vite and Vanilla CSS. The app will faithfully reproduce all 13 reference screens, design tokens, interactive flows, and stateful operations.

---

## 1. Analysis of Reference Screens

From inspecting the 13 PNG files in `./design`:
1. **`Frame 1.png` (Authentication / Sign In)**:
   - Split layout: Left hero banner with satellite imagery, "Clarity when it matters most", 14 districts / 24/7 / Secure statistics.
   - Right form: "Welcome to ResQCore", work email, password, role dropdown (Command Operator, Field Responder, District Administrator), "Remember this device" checkbox, "Sign in to command center" CTA.
2. **`Command Center.png` & `Loading state · Command Center.png` (Operational Overview)**:
   - Sidebar navigation: Brand logo, Command Center (active), Live Map, Incidents (badge 24), Teams, Reports, Communication, Settings, Active incident pill ("Kerala monsoon 2026"), System Online status indicator.
   - Top bar: Breadcrumb ("Command Center | OPERATIONS / KERALA"), Location dropdown ("Ernakulam, Kerala"), Weather widget ("27°C · Heavy rain"), User avatar ("Ananya Kumar, Command Operator").
   - KPI metric cards: Active Incidents (24), People Affected (1,284), Rescue Teams Deployed (12 / 16), Relief Supplies (8,450).
   - Area Intelligence map widget with map/satellite toggle, incident hotspot pins, zoom/pan controls, and active toast ("New High incident: INC-2048 · Flooding in Fort Kochi").
   - Recent Alerts list (Flash flooding, Bridge collapse, Coastal evacuation).
   - Live Camera Feeds with live status indicators and timestamps (Fort Kochi ferry, Mattancherry bridge, Vypin coast road).
   - Loading skeleton state toggle to simulate live sync/data refresh.
3. **`Live Map.png`, `Incident Details · Verify.png`, `Verified · Team assigned.png` (Live Response Map & Verification Flow)**:
   - Full-bleed tactical map view with satellite/vector basemap layers, pinpoint coordinate telemetry (`9.9658° N · 76.2421° E · Zoom 13`), interactive pins colored by severity (High: Red, Medium: Amber, Info: Blue, Deployed: Green).
   - Filter controls: Location search, Severity filter, Status filter, "Show teams" toggle.
   - Right side panel / Incident Details drawer:
     - Header with close button, incident badge (`INC-2048`, `High`), title (`Flash flooding`), location (`Fort Kochi · Ernakulam, Kerala`).
     - Flood site imagery, impact metrics (320 affected, 14:32 IST reported).
     - Field report text, coordinates, verification status pill (`Unverified`).
     - Action button: `Verify incident`.
     - When clicked: Transitions to verified state with green banner `● Verified · Response initiated`, team assignment card (`Bravo 02 · Water rescue · ETA 12 min`), bottom success toast, and updated map pin.
4. **`Incidents.png`, `No team available · Escalated.png`, `Empty state · Incident search.png` (Incident Register)**:
   - Filter bar: Search input, Severity filter, Status filter, Priority sorting, Summary count chips (6 High, 10 Medium, 8 Info).
   - Escalation warning banner: "⚠ No team available - escalated | INC-2047 · Mattancherry bridge collapse · District response notified at 14:30 IST. [View incident ->]".
   - Comprehensive incident table with status badges (`Unverified`, `Escalated`, `Responding`, `On site`, `Monitoring`).
   - Clicking any incident row opens the incident detail drawer on the right.
   - Pagination controls (`Showing 1–6 of 24 incidents`, `1 2 3 4`).
   - Interactive search empty state matching `Empty state · Incident search.png` with "No matching incidents" illustration and "Clear filters" button.
5. **`Teams.png` (Response Teams Hub)**:
   - Status counters (12 deployed, 4 available).
   - Search bar and status/specialization filters, Grid/List view toggle.
   - Team cards for Alpha 01, Bravo 02, Charlie 03, Delta 04, Echo 05, Foxtrot 06 with live radio status, team lead, member count, assignment status, and interactive "Assign" / "View team" modal.
6. **`Communication.png` (Operational Communications & Broadcast)**:
   - Channels list: `# Ernakulam command` (3 unread), `# Field coordination`, `# Relief distribution`, `# Medical response`, Direct Messages.
   - Live chat feed with timeline markers, user messages, and input box with send & attachment buttons.
   - Operational alerts widget and "Send broadcast" composer with recipient selector and severity tagging.
7. **`Reports.png` (Response Intelligence & Analytics)**:
   - 24-hour summary metrics: Incidents recorded (72), People affected (1,284), Average response (18 min), People evacuated (946).
   - Interactive heat concentration map with zone breakdown (Fort Kochi, Mattancherry, Vypin, Edappally).
   - 24-hour incident trend graph (SVG spline curve with time axis).
   - Active incident severity progress distribution.
   - "Export PDF" / Print feature.
8. **`ResQCore · Reusable UI kit.png` (Design System Tokens)**:
   - Exact color tokens:
     - Background: Deep Navy (`#060B14`, `#0A101D`, `#0D1527`, `#111C33`)
     - Borders: `#1E293B`, `#26354D`
     - Primary Accent: Royal Blue (`#2563EB`, `#3B82F6`)
     - High Severity: Crimson Red (`#EF4444`, `#DC2626`, badge `#2C1518`)
     - Medium Severity: Amber/Orange (`#F59E0B`, badge `#2B2011`)
     - Info: Cyan/Blue (`#3B82F6`, badge `#0F1D33`)
     - Deployed/Online: Emerald Green (`#10B981`, badge `#0B251D`)
   - Typography: `Inter`, 8px spatial rhythm, 16px card radiuses.

