## 2. Proposed Architecture & Project Structure

The project will be built with **Vite + React (JavaScript)** and cleanly structured Vanilla CSS for styling:

```
resqcore/
├── index.html
├── package.json
├── vite.config.js
├── public/
│   └── assets/           # Local maps, satellite imagery, flood site photos
├── src/
│   ├── main.jsx
│   ├── App.jsx           # Root route manager & global state provider
│   ├── index.css         # Global design tokens, typography, reset, scrollbars
│   ├── context/
│   │   └── AppContext.jsx # Shared live operational state (incidents, teams, messages, user role)
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── common/
│   │   │   ├── Sidebar.jsx
│   │   │   ├── Topbar.jsx
│   │   │   ├── Badge.jsx
│   │   │   ├── Toast.jsx
│   │   │   └── MapView.jsx      # Interactive SVG/Canvas satellite map with pins & telemetry
│   │   ├── drawers/
│   │   │   └── IncidentDetailDrawer.jsx
│   │   └── modals/
│   │       ├── AssignTeamModal.jsx
│   │       └── BroadcastToast.jsx
│   ├── pages/
│   │   ├── Login.jsx            # Frame 1.png
│   │   ├── CommandCenter.jsx    # Command Center.png & Loading state
│   │   ├── LiveMapPage.jsx      # Live Map.png & Incident Details Verify
│   │   ├── IncidentsPage.jsx    # Incidents.png, Escalated & Empty state
│   │   ├── TeamsPage.jsx        # Teams.png
│   │   ├── CommunicationPage.jsx # Communication.png
│   │   ├── ReportsPage.jsx      # Reports.png
│   │   └── SettingsPage.jsx     # Settings
│   ├── data/
│   │   ├── initialData.js       # All authentic Kerala 2026 data matching reference designs
│   │   └── mockMapData.js       # Geographic pin coordinates, satellite overlays
│   └── styles/
│       ├── layout.css
│       ├── components.css
│       └── pages.css
```

---

## 3. Key Interactive Features & Logic

- **Authentication Flow**: Login screen validation, "Remember this device", role selection (Command Operator, Field Responder, District Administrator), direct seamless login to Command Center, and logout from profile avatar.
- **Incident Verification Flow**:
  - Clicking `INC-2048` opens the Incident Details drawer.
  - Clicking "Verify incident" transitions the status to `Verified`, assigns team `Bravo 02` (ETA 12 min), fires the "Team assigned" toast, and updates the incident badge across the map and table.
- **Escalation Notification**:
  - Banner alert for `INC-2047` (Mattancherry bridge collapse), clicking "View incident" focuses `INC-2047` and displays the escalated state.
- **Team Assignment**:
  - On the Teams page, clicking "Assign" on `Bravo 02` or `Charlie 03` opens an assignment modal allowing the user to dispatch them to an active incident.
- **Live Communication**:
  - Switch channels (`# Ernakulam command`, `# Field coordination`, direct messages).
  - Send messages in real time (appended to conversation).
  - Send emergency broadcasts with instant operational alerts toast.
- **Filtering & Search**:
  - Real-time search by location or incident ID in Incidents, Map, and Teams.
  - Severity filter (`All`, `High`, `Medium`, `Info`).
  - Status filter (`All`, `Unverified`, `Escalated`, `Responding`, `On site`, `Monitoring`).
  - Demonstrates the empty state when no matching results are found, with a working "Clear filters" button.
- **Interactive Map**:
  - Toggle between Satellite view and Map view.
  - Zoom controls (+ / -) and Reset view button.
  - Clickable pins with hover tooltips and selection states matching the Figma UI.
- **Data Persistence**:
  - State changes (verification, team assignment, messages) persist in memory across all page tabs during the session.

